    coal_fuel_inventory: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-16 (miso-259) WITH the field \u2014 U: UNTESTED here, and the field RAISES rather than silently skipping if armed for this ISO. The chartering measurement is MISO's own coal stock and receipts footprint; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean MISO's verdict fills no other ISO's cell. The datatypes are NATIONAL and the read-time join is ISO-agnostic, so a coal ISO arming this needs no new intake \u2014 but it must derive its own footprint, its own delivery-rate construction and its own shared-storage reconciliation from its own market's data, and lift the MISO gate deliberately." },
    hydro_cascade_coupling: { cell: "O", ev: "NWPP-36 (2026-09-16) BUILT, MEASURED, ARMED AT TEST SCALE, NOT YET SOLVED ON THE FOOTPRINT \u2014 O: OPEN (the arm-for-NWPP-40 decision is the owner's, rule 31). Owner ruling N3 put this ahead of the first keeper. THE MEASUREMENT (PRECOMMIT \u00a74, CROHMS hourly 2023-2025 + NID + EIA-923, all quality-0): tau by cross-correlation of outflow anomalies \u2014 GCL->CHJ 0 h (r 0.84), CHJ->WEL 1 h (0.48), RRH->RIS 1 h (0.93), TDA->BON 0 h (0.43), LMN->IHR 0 h (0.74), and the pooled reaches WAN->PRD, MCN->JDA, JDA->TDA, LWG->LGS, LGS->LMN all 0 h (0.63-0.88), PRD->MCN 13 h / IHR->MCN 0 h (joint 2-D, 0.35); operated pondage bands 1.9-6.4 ft (BPA's published order is 3-5 ft), 89-2,003 kcfs\u00b7h. TEN OF FIFTEEN LINKS FAIL A PRE-REGISTERED GATE AND ARE LEFT UNCOUPLED, never substituted: WEL->RRH implied celerity 34.9 mph (>30), RIS->WAN 2023 tau 23 h vs 2024 0 h (a diurnal alias), DWR->LWG r 0.02 (Dworshak is ~10 % of Lower Granite's inflow), and SEVEN links (RRH, WAN->PRD, PRD/IHR->MCN, MCN->JDA, JDA->TDA, LWG->LGS, LGS->LMN) trip the 2 % side-inflow floor in spill-season months \u2014 the downstream project's metered outflow runs 2-8 % BELOW its upstream's in Apr-Aug, a spill-metering artefact at the federal lower-river projects (The Dalles/John Day 0.970 annual). RESULT: FIVE coupled plants (CHJ, WEL, RIS, BON, IHR; 5,717 MW = 16 % of NWPP hydro nameplate) below two heads and three uncoupled upstreams whose measured monthly-mean spill enters the RHS. GATE G8: all 25 keeper/default cache keys byte-identical base 6d1a144d -> head; LP sha256-identical OFF, differs ARMED. ARMED TEST (real chain, one-zone reduced system, Jan + May 2023, tests/unit/model/test_hydro_cascade.py): G-A1 PASS (every coupled plant's monthly energy 0.000 % moved \u2014 the rule-19 invariant), G-A2 PASS (identity to 1e-5), G-A4 PASS (May LP spill at BON/IHR within \u00b110 % of measured CROHMS spill; Jan spill under measured + 5 %), G-A5 PASS (lag signature), **G-A3 FAIL as pre-registered**: within-day amplitude falls 1-10 % (CHJ 2.34->2.13, IHR 4.28->3.83), not >= 30 %, because a coupled plant INHERITS its upstream's shape \u2014 Grand Coulee's own amplitude falls 3.71->2.15 as the row transmits Chief Joseph's turbine capacity back up the chain \u2014 and the flat-arrivals peak bound was the wrong premise. Ponds never fill at test scale (one price signal). Evidence: PRECOMMIT-nwpp-36-2026-09-16.md; FINDING-nwpp-36-2026-09-16.md; data/raw/nwpp-hydro/nwpp_hydro_cascade_{links,monthly,nid}.csv." },
