    wecc_endogenous_node: { cell: ".", ev: "NWPP-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row NWPP-21) — n/a: TWO independent reasons, and the second is the one a later lane must not lose. (1) The object is CAISO's own `WECC_import` zone (`iso_configs.py` :533/:570/:573 + its two `TransferLink`s under the 7,500 MW simultaneous cap), a CAISO market object — every non-owner ISO reads `.` at HEAD. (2) NWPP gets NO IMPORT NODE of its own: its seams are served schedules, so neither `IMPORT_TRANCHES` nor `IMPORT_ZONE` takes an NWPP key and `build_import_generators(\"NWPP\") == []` (plan §3 recorded defaults; gate G7). STATED SO IT STAYS VISIBLE, NOT ADJUDICATED HERE: card N4 measures that CAISO's `WECC_import` counterparty IS this footprint — `model/interchange/caiso.py`:443 names its firm tranches `PNW_hydro_base` / `DSW_solar_PV` — so registering NWPP puts the same physical energy on both sides of a seam, represented two ways. Rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] forbids this desk touching how CAISO prices its side and it does not; the CAISO-side question is ROUTED to the CAISO lane. Not a verdict; a later lane that identifies an NWPP analogue re-opens it as U." },
