    state_carbon_pricing: { cell: "U", ev: "NWPP-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/nwpp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row NWPP-21) — U, AND THIS IS THE ONE CELL WHERE NWPP DIVERGES FROM THE SPP SEED THIS SHARD WAS EMITTED AGAINST. SPP reads `.` here on the ground that no state in its footprint carries a carbon programme. That reason does not hold for NWPP: Washington's Climate Commitment Act cap-and-invest programme has been in effect since 2023-01-01 — inside the 2023–2025 scored window — and covers in-state electricity generation and imported electricity, and WA is the footprint's largest state by capacity (31,711.8 MW of 98,738.1 MW, plan §2.1). So an NWPP allowance cost in dispatch is a real candidate object, not a structural absence, and `.` would be the stronger claim made falsely. U is the weaker, correct call. NOTHING IS ASSERTED ABOUT MAGNITUDE, COVERAGE OR PRICE: the programme's registry values and its in-window applicability are NWPP-12's to transcribe with URL + page (plan §6 row 9 discipline), and until then no lane may arm this from memory. Note also plan §2.3's `test_iso_coverage` row expects carbon-`None` at registration — that is a W2 default, not an adjudication of this cell." },
